    <node id="Health Promotion Levy">
      <data key="d0">Health Promotion Levy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Alternative funding sources like the Health Promotion Levy are being explored to maximize the impact of available resources for diabetes prevention and control.&lt;SEP&gt;Health Promotion Levy is a revenue source that can be used to fund diabetes prevention and care programs in South Africa.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46d94ad4db28a87f2b14b78eb3e34260&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809adfa0a14ab6fe4990c753d1ffe33e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754890550</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Clinical Associates">
      <data key="d0">Clinical Associates</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Clinical Associates are healthcare workers involved in diabetes management and care, who may need training enhancement according to the summit recommendations.&lt;SEP&gt;Clinical Associates support care coordination within multidisciplinary teams for diabetes management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f547c1ef7d9fdc3451e37273a2a2eb2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809adfa0a14ab6fe4990c753d1ffe33e</data>
