      <data key="d0">Unhealthy Diet</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">"Unhealthy diet is a behavioral risk factor for non-communicable diseases (NCDs</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2dfcaafdf6869d58b44b99d634f7e8f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754890553</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Limited resources for diabetes prevention and awareness">
      <data key="d0">Limited resources for diabetes prevention and awareness</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This category refers to insufficient budgets and mandates for diabetes awareness and prevention initiatives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c87b51ba48af7d085119b219b21046f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754890553</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lack of post-natal screening for Type 2 diabetes for women with gestational diabetes">
      <data key="d0">Lack of post-natal screening for Type 2 diabetes for women with gestational diabetes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This category highlights the missed opportunity in monitoring women who had diabetes during pregnancy, leading to potential late diagnosis of Type 2 diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c87b51ba48af7d085119b219b21046f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754890553</data>
    </node>
    <node id="South Africa">
      <data key="d0">South Africa</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">South Africa is a country where nutritional challenges such as obesity and underweight conditions are prevalent, influencing national health policies.&lt;SEP&gt;South Africa is a country where the book's message on healthy eating and reducing salt intake has relevance, particularly for addressing high blood pressure issues.&lt;SEP&gt;South Africa, a country grappling with substantial challenges in diabetes surveillance, management, research, and care, serves as the central geographical context for discussions on improving diabetes prevention and control. These challenges are multifaceted, involving issues such as workforce integration and resource allocation. Despite these obstacles, efforts like those of the Diabetes Alliance are focused on enhancing diabetes care within the country. Additionally, significant limitations in academic institutions and dedicated researchers further complicate the landscape of diabetes management in South Africa. The challenges identified during the Diabetes Summit reflect ongoing concerns and areas for improvement in the country's approach to diabetes care.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1bbcda5be08e321e58b42b986d804d9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d94ad4db28a87f2b14b78eb3e34260&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-809adfa0a14ab6fe4990c753d1ffe33e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f547c1ef7d9fdc3451e37273a2a2eb2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d396dda3ce9b0c2f87b5d6ddb9d013b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c3dada45a598da1af9a6c9dc041e660&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a58ab095e62951eddfd80f0a0e2848&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a3470aab48da10bd8a36978481943e4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754897478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Carbs">
      <data key="d0">Carbs</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Carbohydrates are found in starchy foods like pasta, rice, potatoes, bread and pap, and are often consumed in excessive amounts."&lt;&lt;关系描述&gt;&gt;"Description not available in text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6699a5c79683213ff4dea6e14b493c72</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754890553</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health Promotion Levy (HPL)">
      <data key="d0">Health Promotion Levy (HPL)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The HPL is a 10% tax on sugar-sweetened beverages implemented in South Africa in 2018, aimed at generating revenue to combat diabetes through funding prevention programmes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c87b51ba48af7d085119b219b21046f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754890553</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Nuts and Seeds">
      <data key="d0">Nuts and Seeds</data>
      <data key="d1">food</data>
      <data key="d2">Raw, unsalted nuts and seeds are better options compared to salty snacks like chips for managing carb intake while providing important nutrients."&lt;&lt;关系描述&gt;&gt;"Healthy snacking, nutritional value</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6699a5c79683213ff4dea6e14b493c72</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754890553</data>
    </node>
    <node id="White Bread">
      <data key="d0">White Bread</data>
      <data key="d1">food</data>
      <data key="d2">White bread lacks the fiber content of whole grain options like whole wheat or brown bread but is often chosen due to its softer texture."&lt;&lt;关系描述&gt;&gt;"Comparison with healthier alternatives, portion control</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6699a5c79683213ff4dea6e14b493c72</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754890553</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sweet Potatoes">
      <data key="d0">Sweet Potatoes</data>
      <data key="d1">food</data>
      <data key="d2">Sweet potatoes are recommended as a starchy vegetable alternative to white rice or potatoes, providing better health benefits.&lt;SEP&gt;Sweet potatoes are recommended over regular white potatoes as they have a lower glycemic index and provide more nutrients."&lt;&lt;关系描述&gt;&gt;"Nutritional value, blood sugar management</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd33b3de797d4c6bf9bce23ddb306beb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6699a5c79683213ff4dea6e14b493c72</data>
