    </node>
    <node id="maltose">
      <data key="d0">maltose</data>
      <data key="d1">ingredient</data>
      <data key="d2">Maltose is a disaccharide sugar derived from the breakdown of starch; it's used for its sweetness and texturizing properties in food products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b79825bf243d6abdec856f313bda4e9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754890575</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Rights Approach to Diabetes Funding">
      <data key="d0">Human Rights Approach to Diabetes Funding</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Viewing diabetes through a human rights lens emphasizes the need for increased investments due to significant human suffering caused by undiagnosed and poorly managed diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46d94ad4db28a87f2b14b78eb3e34260</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754890575</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Collaboration with Regional and Global Partners">
      <data key="d0">Collaboration with Regional and Global Partners</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Partnering with regional and global organizations like the WHO or Africa CDC can provide technical expertise and support for reducing the diabetes burden through cost-effective solutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-46d94ad4db28a87f2b14b78eb3e34260</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1754890576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="isomaltose">
      <data key="d0">isomaltose</data>
      <data key="d1">ingredient</data>
      <data key="d2">Isomaltose, a sugar found naturally in some plants, can be added to foods as a sweetener with a lower glycemic index compared to other sugars.</data>
