    <node id="Butternut">
      <data key="d0">Butternut</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Butternut is a type of vegetable known for its orange flesh and sweet taste, commonly used in various recipes such as Butternut &amp; Lentil Cottage Pie and Chicken &amp; Broccoli Bake. Descriptions indicate that butternut is typically peeled and cubed before being added to the pot, often after being fried with spices. While it can be substituted for sweet potatoes in certain recipes, butternut's versatility allows it to be used in a variety of dishes where its rich flavor and texture are desired.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1bea3aa6519bdbc96a177e5b01313158&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e546234b6e9b258b1e7e54862eaa666f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bd7d456fa9b5f0c564afd5dd3bb0af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25e31297f3300051fe4ba3bfefc44fd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c30d19cfece6de65df0c2321c6c977c5</data>
