    <node id="Lentils">
      <data key="d0">Lentils</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Lentils, often categorized under legumes, are commonly utilized as a meat substitute in various culinary applications. These versatile legumes can effectively replace meat in family meals and are particularly suitable for dishes such as lasagne, bolognaise, or meatballs. In the Butternut &amp; Lentil Cottage Pie recipe, lentils are appreciated not only for their ability to mimic the texture of meat but also for their health benefits. Additionally, lentils are used in side dishes, with a specific recipe provided for brown lentils seasoned with herbs, highlighting their diverse culinary uses and nutritional value.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-25e31297f3300051fe4ba3bfefc44fd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-432b00aa4a62ed1cc5b80a9b6a970a9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baf922dec0d429fd4c06191ccab7f11c</data>
