      <data key="d11">1754890640</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10 Guidelines" target="healthy eating">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The guidelines are specifically aimed at promoting healthy eating habits.</data>
      <data key="d8">guidelines,nutrition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ab7e41bfc6dc460c48107220733a6cc</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890637</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="healthy eating" target="diabetes">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Maintaining a healthy diet is important for managing diabetes and preventing its complications.</data>
      <data key="d8">diet management,prevention</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ab7e41bfc6dc460c48107220733a6cc</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890638</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="healthy eating" target="plant-based meals">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Plant-based meals are recommended to support healthy eating habits based on the guidelines provided in Annexure I.</data>
      <data key="d8">8</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-fb7f9553a2f42b8058dc0445b5667f49</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754897519</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="protein" target="fibre">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Both protein and fiber are mentioned as components found in dry beans, split peas, lentils, or soya.</data>
      <data key="d8">dietary components,nutrient pairs</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ab7e41bfc6dc460c48107220733a6cc</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890638</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bad fats" target="lean meat">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Lean or lower fat options of meat are recommended as alternatives to meats high in bad (saturated) fats.</data>
      <data key="d8">dietary choices,health implications</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ab7e41bfc6dc460c48107220733a6cc</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890638</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="dairy products" target="milk">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Milk is a specific type of dairy product recommended for its nutritional benefits.</data>
      <data key="d8">dietary component,type relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ab7e41bfc6dc460c48107220733a6cc</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890638</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sugar" target="chronic diseases">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Eating too much sugar can lead to chronic diseases, emphasizing its importance in dietary management.</data>
      <data key="d8">health risks,nutrition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ab7e41bfc6dc460c48107220733a6cc</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890639</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sugar" target="brown sugar">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Brown sugar is one of the many types of sugars that can appear on a label, as detailed in the text.</data>
      <data key="d8">8</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7b79825bf243d6abdec856f313bda4e9</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890656</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sugar" target="home-cooked meals">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Home-cooked meals generally contain less sugar than processed foods and restaurant meals, promoting a healthier diet.</data>
      <data key="d8">7</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-fb7f9553a2f42b8058dc0445b5667f49</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754897517</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fats" target="unsaturated fats">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Unsaturated fats are recommended to replace bad fats like those found in butter and hard margarine.</data>
      <data key="d8">dietary choices,health implications</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4ab7e41bfc6dc460c48107220733a6cc</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890639</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Hypoglycaemia">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">People with Type 2 Diabetes can experience hypoglycaemia due to low blood sugar levels, which may occur from skipping meals or incorrect medication dosing.</data>
      <data key="d8">complication,condition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890639</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Hyperglycaemia">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Uncontrolled Type 2 Diabetes can lead to hyperglycaemia when blood glucose levels rise too high over several days. This may result in the production of ketones and ketoacidosis if not managed properly.</data>
      <data key="d8">complication,condition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890640</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Ketoacidosis">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Uncontrolled Type 1 or severe cases of Type 2 Diabetes can lead to ketoacidosis due to the production of ketones from fat breakdown. Regular management is crucial to avoid this life-threatening condition.</data>
      <data key="d8">complication,condition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890640</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Impaired Glucose Tolerance">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Impaired Glucose Tolerance can develop into Type 2 Diabetes if lifestyle factors such as diet and exercise are not improved. It serves as a warning sign for potential progression.</data>
      <data key="d8">condition,risk factor</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890641</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Gestational Diabetes (GDM)">
      <data key="d6">5.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Women who have experienced Gestational Diabetes during pregnancy are at an increased risk of developing Type 2 Diabetes later in life. Regular monitoring is advised to prevent progression.</data>
      <data key="d8">condition,risk factor</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890641</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Pre-diabetes">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Pre-diabetes can progress to Type 2 Diabetes if lifestyle factors such as diet and exercise are not improved. Early detection and management are crucial for prevention.</data>
      <data key="d8">condition,risk factor</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890642</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Healthy Eating Habits">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Managing diabetes effectively requires maintaining healthy eating habits to control blood glucose levels. This is a key aspect of lifestyle changes needed for better management.</data>
      <data key="d8">lifestyle change,management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890642</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Regular Exercise">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Regular exercise is crucial in the management of diabetes by improving insulin sensitivity and overall health. It complements other treatments like medication to control blood glucose levels.</data>
      <data key="d8">lifestyle change,management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890643</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Oral Medication">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Oral medication is one form of treatment for Type 2 Diabetes that helps manage blood glucose levels when combined with lifestyle changes. It can be used to control symptoms effectively.</data>
      <data key="d8">management,treatment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890643</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Insulin Injections">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">In severe cases or where oral medication is insufficient, insulin injections are a common treatment method for managing blood glucose levels in people living with Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d8">management,treatment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890644</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Routine Blood or Urine Glucose Test">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Routine blood or urine glucose tests are often used to diagnose Type 2 Diabetes when high levels of sugar in the blood are detected. This is a common method for early detection.</data>
      <data key="d8">diagnosis,screening</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890645</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Blood Sugar Levels">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Managing Type 2 Diabetes involves closely monitoring and controlling blood sugar levels to prevent complications. Blood sugar tests are a key part of this management strategy.</data>
      <data key="d8">control,management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890645</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Insulin Resistance">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">People with insulin resistance are at a higher risk of developing Type 2 Diabetes as their body's cells do not respond effectively to insulin, leading to high blood sugar levels.</data>
      <data key="d8">progression,risk factor</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890646</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Healthy Diet">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Maintaining a healthy diet is essential for managing Type 2 Diabetes by helping to control blood glucose levels and improve overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d8">lifestyle,management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890646</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Physical Activity">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Regular physical activity is crucial for managing Type 2 Diabetes as it can improve insulin sensitivity and help control blood glucose levels. It complements other treatment methods.</data>
      <data key="d8">lifestyle,management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890647</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Healthcare Professional">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A healthcare professional plays a crucial role in managing Type 2 Diabetes by providing advice on treatment options, dietary guidelines, exercise recommendations, and regular monitoring.</data>
      <data key="d8">management,support</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890647</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Ketoacidosis (Type 1 Diabetes)">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">While ketoacidosis is more common in Type 1 Diabetes, understanding it can help manage blood sugar levels and prevent severe complications that can occur in both types of diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d8">prevention,risk awareness</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890648</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Lower Limb Amputations">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Poorly managed Type 2 Diabetes can lead to severe complications such as lower limb amputations if blood circulation and nerve damage are not addressed.</data>
      <data key="d8">complication,prevention</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890649</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Blood Vessel Damage">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High blood sugar levels over time lead to damage in blood vessels, affecting various organs and increasing the risk of heart disease and other complications.</data>
      <data key="d8">complication,prevention</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890650</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Healthy Diet and Exercise">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Both healthy diet and regular exercise are essential for managing Type 2 Diabetes. They help control blood sugar levels and improve overall health.</data>
      <data key="d8">lifestyle,management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890650</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Oral Medication and Insulin Injections">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Both oral medication and insulin injections are treatment methods used to manage Type 2 Diabetes. They can be used individually or in combination based on the severity of the condition.</data>
      <data key="d8">management,treatment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890651</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Exercise Program">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Starting an exercise program benefits people with Type 2 diabetes by helping them lose weight and manage insulin production effectively.</data>
      <data key="d8">improved insulin utilization,weight management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f5fc341d7bf2fb8dcae642731ec8fb0d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890652</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Smoking">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Smokers with Type 2 diabetes have a higher risk of heart disease and other complications due to smoking's impact on blood vessels.</data>
      <data key="d8">cardiovascular risks,vascular damage</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f5fc341d7bf2fb8dcae642731ec8fb0d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890652</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="Home Blood Sugar Monitor">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Using a home blood sugar monitor allows individuals to better manage their diabetes by monitoring glucose levels.</data>
      <data key="d8">improved management,self-monitoring</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f5fc341d7bf2fb8dcae642731ec8fb0d</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890654</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hyperglycaemia" target="Nausea and Vomiting">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High blood glucose levels can lead to symptoms such as nausea and vomiting. Monitoring these symptoms is important for managing diabetes effectively.</data>
      <data key="d8">management,symptom</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890645</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ketoacidosis" target="Ketone Strips">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Using ketone strips is essential for monitoring and managing ketoacidosis, a serious condition caused by high levels of ketones in the bloodstream.</data>
      <data key="d8">detection,management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-129a310c5d71871c9ee11cf249dcb6c3</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890643</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Healthy Eating Habits" target="Blood Sugar Levels">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Controlling the intake of carbohydrates, including starches and sugars, through healthy eating habits helps manage blood sugar levels.</data>
      <data key="d8">blood sugar control,nutritional management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c6dac05970727d54d46abd86982b759</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890647</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Physical Activity" target="Blood Sugar Levels">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Regular physical activity helps improve blood glucose control and overall health for people with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d8">blood sugar management,exercise</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c6dac05970727d54d46abd86982b759</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890649</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Portion Sizes" target="Carbohydrates">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Managing portion sizes is crucial for controlling carbohydrate intake, which directly affects blood sugar levels.</data>
      <data key="d8">blood sugar management,portion control</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c6dac05970727d54d46abd86982b759</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890647</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Portion Sizes" target="Nutritional Value">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Eating a variety of foods in appropriate portions ensures nutritional value while managing calorie and carbohydrate intake.</data>
      <data key="d8">nutritional balance,portion control</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c6dac05970727d54d46abd86982b759</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890648</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Sugar Levels" target="Fruits">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Some fruits contain natural sugars but should be managed as part of overall carbohydrate intake to control blood sugar levels.</data>
      <data key="d8">fruit consumption,sugar management</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c6dac05970727d54d46abd86982b759</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890648</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Sugar Levels" target="Diabetes Management">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Both focus on controlling blood sugar levels as part of managing diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d8">7</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-520eb52d6ccc68c424c497fa7e6df29a</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890663</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Carbohydrates" target="Starches and Sugars">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Starches and sugars are types of carbohydrates that have a significant impact on blood sugar levels.</data>
      <data key="d8">blood sugar effect,carbohydrate classification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-3c6dac05970727d54d46abd86982b759</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1754890648</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Starches" target="Diabetes">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">When planning meals, it is important to consider carbohydrate intake, especially for those with diabetes, as starchy foods can contribute significantly.</data>
